Lunchtime is approaching.
My first shift at the café has finished.
I untie my apron and put it away.
I go to Sunita ji.
"Thank you very much for so much patience," I say.
"Today I have learned a lot from you."
Sunita ji smiles affectionately.
"You did very good work, Maya," she says.
"Now go home and rest."
I step out of the café.
My flat is nearby from here.
So I walk towards home on foot.
After work, I have gotten very tired.
There is a little pain in my legs.
But I am feeling very happy.
Today I have learned to make coffee with the espresso machine.
My first coffee was bad, but the second coffee turned out good.
I really liked serving this community.
